        "summary":  "Google Research and Google DeepMind published findings on AMIE, a multimodal research AI system built on Gemini and Project Astra, capable of conducting real-time video medical consultations by interpreting visual cues, auditory signals, and diagnostic reasoning in real time. In a randomized study using patient actors and physician evaluators, AMIE achieved expert-level ratings across diagnostic accuracy, history-taking, and communication quality. The system remains experimental and is not yet cleared for clinical deployment.",
        "execSummary":  "AMIE represents a significant research milestone: an AI system that can perform a structured medical consultation end-to-end, including visual diagnosis, at expert physician equivalence in controlled trials. For healthcare enterprise leaders, this is a bellwether for where AI-assisted care is heading within a 3ΓÇô5 year horizon, even if clinical deployment is still years away. Organizations in health systems, insurance, or employer health benefits should begin mapping which consultation workflows could be augmented or triaged by systems like AMIE before competitors do. The dependency on Gemini and Project Astra infrastructure makes this a strong signal of Google\u0027s intent to be the foundation model layer for healthcare AI.",
